---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout>
  <section class="hero">
    <div>
      <div class="hero-kicker">Local-first vector studio</div>
      <h1>Draw.<br />Import.<br /><em>Export.</em></h1>
      <p>
        Bird is a complete vector editor in the browser: Bézier pen, layers,
        rulers and guides, Pathfinder, editable text, multiple artboards,
        <b>SVG · PDF · AI · EPS</b> import and <b>SVG, PDF or PDF/X-1a</b> export.
        No install, no account, your documents stay with you.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="cta" href="/editor">Open the editor</a>
        <a class="cta cta--ghost" href="/docs">Read the documentation</a>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-note">Free · local-first · PWA · desktop app for macOS, Windows and Linux</div>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-card" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="hero-card-head">
        <span class="dot"></span><span class="dot"></span><span class="dot"></span>
        <span class="hero-card-title">bird / untitled</span>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-card-body">
        <div class="artboard-mock"></div>
        <div class="mock-tools">
          <span class="mock-tool on"></span>
          <span class="mock-tool"></span><span class="mock-tool"></span>
          <span class="mock-tool"></span><span class="mock-tool"></span>
          <span class="mock-tool"></span><span class="mock-tool"></span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="features">
    <div class="section-head">
      <div>
        <h2>Everything a real vector editor must do</h2>
        <p>Not a demo: a complete workshop, built to produce files that printers and design tools can actually use.</p>
      </div>
      <span>01 — Features</span>
    </div>
    <div class="features">
      <article class="feature"><span class="feature-num">01</span><h3>Bézier pen</h3><p>Editable anchors and handles, curved segments, closing, re-editing any path.</p></article>
      <article class="feature"><span class="feature-num">02</span><h3>Layers</h3><p>Select, rename, hide, lock and reorder objects. The organisation of a real document.</p></article>
      <article class="feature"><span class="feature-num">03</span><h3>Rulers &amp; guides</h3><p>Live rulers, draggable guides, grid and snapping to edges, centres and objects.</p></article>
      <article class="feature"><span class="feature-num">04</span><h3>Pathfinder</h3><p>Vector union, subtract, intersect and exclude — no rasterisation.</p></article>
      <article class="feature"><span class="feature-num">05</span><h3>PDF / AI import</h3><p>Modern .ai files are PDFs: Bird opens them as editable Fabric objects. A multi-page PDF gives one artboard per page.</p></article>
      <article class="feature"><span class="feature-num">06</span><h3>EPS import</h3><p>Adobe Illustrator level 2 PostScript interpreter: paths, colours, clips, curves.</p></article>
      <article class="feature"><span class="feature-num">07</span><h3>PDF/X-1a for printers</h3><p>CMYK, ICC profiles, gradients as real shadings, text as outlines, bleed. The file a printer accepts.</p></article>
      <article class="feature"><span class="feature-num">08</span><h3>SVG &amp; raster export</h3><p>SVG of the document or the selection, multi-artboard PDF, transparent PNG, JPG, WEBP, 1× to 4× scales.</p></article>
      <article class="feature"><span class="feature-num">09</span><h3>Editable text</h3><p>Fonts, sizes, bold, italic, underline, strikethrough, alignment. Text stays text, or becomes outlines on request.</p></article>
      <article class="feature"><span class="feature-num">10</span><h3>Incremental undo</h3><p>Each state stores only the objects that changed: 50 undos cost the price of a single save.</p></article>
      <article class="feature"><span class="feature-num">11</span><h3>Detachable panels</h3><p>Every section of the right panel becomes a floating window, movable and remembered.</p></article>
      <article class="feature"><span class="feature-num">12</span><h3>Multiple artboards</h3><p>Like Illustrator artboards: independent format, floating switcher, history per artboard.</p></article>
      <article class="feature"><span class="feature-num">13</span><h3>Plug-ins</h3><p>One <code>.plugin.js</code> file is enough: registry, generated settings panel, vector pattern included.</p></article>
      <article class="feature"><span class="feature-num">14</span><h3>Desktop app</h3><p>macOS, Windows and Linux: system menu with Adobe/Figma shortcuts and native files.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="formats">
    <div class="section-head">
      <div>
        <h2>Import / export: the formats that matter</h2>
        <p>Detected by signature (not just by extension), with systematic cleaning of imported content.</p>
      </div>
      <span>02 — Exchange</span>
    </div>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Format</th><th>Direction</th><th>Engine</th><th>Result</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><b>SVG / SVGZ</b></td><td>Import</td><td>Fabric + sanitizer</td><td>Editable vector objects</td></tr>
          <tr><td><b>PDF</b></td><td>Import</td><td>pdf.js 3.11</td><td>Paths, clips, colours, text, images — multi-page</td></tr>
          <tr><td><b>Adobe Illustrator .ai</b></td><td>Import</td><td>PDF or PostScript</td><td>Editable vectors</td></tr>
          <tr><td><b>EPS</b></td><td>Import</td><td>PostScript interpreter</td><td>Fabric paths</td></tr>
          <tr><td><b>SVG</b></td><td>Export</td><td>Fabric</td><td>Document or selection, background of your choice</td></tr>
          <tr><td><b>PDF</b></td><td>Export</td><td>svg2pdf + jsPDF</td><td>Vector PDF, Illustrator-compatible</td></tr>
          <tr><td><b>PDF/X-1a</b></td><td>Export</td><td>Built-in writer</td><td>CMYK, real shadings, ICC, text as outlines</td></tr>
          <tr><td><b>PNG / JPG / WEBP</b></td><td>Export</td><td>Canvas</td><td>Raster 1×–4×, transparency or white background</td></tr>
          <tr><td><b>.plume</b></td><td>Project</td><td>JSON v3</td><td>Full document + artboards + guides</td></tr>
          <tr><td><b>.dmg / .msi / .deb</b></td><td>Desktop</td><td>Tauri 2</td><td>Native app for macOS, Windows, Linux</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="versions">
    <div class="section-head">
      <div>
        <h2>Four builds, one engine</h2>
        <p>The same vector core, available as a standalone web page, an Astro site, a Rust toolkit and a desktop app.</p>
      </div>
      <span>03 — Versions</span>
    </div>
    <div class="versions">
      <article class="version-card">
        <span class="version-tag">Web</span>
        <h3>Standalone Bird</h3>
        <p>A single <code>index.html</code>, no build step. Perfect for a shared folder or a USB stick.</p>
        <a class="cta cta--ghost" href="/editor">Open</a>
      </article>
      <article class="version-card">
        <span class="version-tag">Astro</span>
        <h3>Site &amp; PWA</h3>
        <p>SEO pages, API routes, OpenRouter proxy, sitemap and service worker. The engine is synchronised automatically.</p>
        <a class="cta cta--ghost" href="/docs#astro">Documentation</a>
      </article>
      <article class="version-card">
        <span class="version-tag">Rust</span>
        <h3>Native engine</h3>
        <p>CLI and local server: inspect projects, convert SVG/PDF/EPS, validate .plume files.</p>
        <a class="cta cta--ghost" href="/docs#rust">Documentation</a>
      </article>
      <article class="version-card">
        <span class="version-tag">Desktop</span>
        <h3>macOS · Windows · Linux</h3>
        <p>Tauri shell: system menu with Adobe/Figma shortcuts, native files, signable installers.</p>
        <a class="cta cta--ghost" href="/docs#desktop">Documentation</a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>